68 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Intersection detection is a fundamental operation in the 2D Arrangement package, but it poses significant challenges in terms of efficiency and robustness. The current implementation relies on traits classes that provide specialized logic for different curve families, leading to variations in performance and complexity. As the diversity of supported curves increases, intersection computations become computationally expensive due to: a. Redundant calculations during repeated intersection checks b. Lack of unified optimization strategies across curve types c. Handling of degenerate and edge cases \(e.g., overlapping curves, tangential intersections\) Additionally, robustness issues may arise due to numerical precision limitations and inconsistencies in handling special geometric configurations. These challenges can negatively impact the overall performance and reliability of applications built on top of CGAL.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
69 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (This project aims to improve both the efficiency and robustness of curve intersection computations in CGAL by optimizing the underlying geometric operations within the traits classes.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (The proposed solution includes: Algorithmic Optimization: Introducing more efficient intersection strategies such as filtering techniques \(e.g., bounding box checks\) to eliminate unnecessary computations before performing exact calculations. Refinement of Traits Classes: Enhancing the design and implementation of traits class functors to reduce redundancy and improve consistency across different curve families. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
