77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (The proposed improvements to curve intersection computations in CGAL are expected to have a significant impact on both the performance and reliability of geometric processing workflows. Improved Performance: By reducing redundant computations and introducing optimized intersection strategies, the project will significantly decrease the time required for geometric operations in the 2D Arrangement package. This is especially beneficial for large-scale inputs involving complex curve arrangements. Enhanced Robustness: Strengthening the handling of degenerate and edge cases will improve numerical stability and ensure consistent behavior across different curve families, reducing the likelihood of computational errors. Scalability Across Applications: Faster and more reliable geometric operations will directly benefit applications in computer graphics, CAD systems, GIS, and robotics, where CGAL is widely used for precise geometric computations. Better Developer Experience: Cleaner and more consistent traits class implementations will make the codebase easier to understand, maintain, and extend for future contributors. Long-Term Contribution to CGAL: The optimizations introduced through this project will integrate into the core library, providing lasting value to the open-source community and enabling future enhancements in geometric algorithm design.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
