<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (and data structures, along with a growing interest in computational geometry and algorithm optimization. I am comfortable working with modern C++ \(C++17\) and have experience with problem-solving that involves efficiency and correctness, which are critical for geometric computations. I have a keen interest in understanding complex systems and improving their performance. This aligns well with the goals of CGAL, where both efficiency and robustness are essential. I am particularly motivated to work on low-level geometric operations, as they form the backbone of many real-world applications. Additionally, I am familiar with version control tools like Git and follow a disciplined development approach that includes testing, debugging, and writing maintainable code. I am committed to actively communicating with mentors, incorporating feedback, and ensuring steady progress throughout the coding period. Beyond the GSoC timeline, I am interested in continuing my contributions to CGAL and further exploring computational geometry, making this not just a short-term project but a long-term engagement.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
